Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 12:00:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] (be) ck-phdr-unwind libunwind capture_into_slot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the variant TU `be/src/service/http/action/print_stack_ck_phdr_unwind.cpp`. The handler-side hook copies the interrupted thread's `ucontext_t` into a libunwind context, calls `unw_init_local2` with `UNW_INIT_SIGNAL_FRAME`, and walks via `unw_get_reg(UNW_REG_IP)` + `unw_step` up to `kMaxSignalFrames`.

No `hasPHDRCache()` gate. CK runs the same shape under TSan in its CI (tests/queries/0_stateless/03565_system_stack_trace_works.sh has no `no-tsan` tag) and `StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp` calls `StackTrace(signal_context)` — which goes to `unw_backtrace` — unconditionally. CK reserves `hasPHDRCache()` for the `trace_log` continuous sampler boot decision in `programs/server/Server.cpp:1339`. A gate at one capture site cannot meaningfully protect the process when exception unwinding, jemalloc backtracing, and other `dl_iterate_phdr` callers run unguarded.

`UNW_LOCAL_ONLY` is defined before `<libunwind.h>` so the include resolves to the local-only `_ULx86_64_*` symbols the Doris libunwind archive exports. `be/src/service/CMakeLists.txt` globs `*.cpp` recursively, so the new TU is picked up without a CMakeLists edit.

Spec: docs/architecture.md "Layer 3d"; docs/design/ck.md "Decisions", "Shape", "Workflow".

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
